      "title": "Malformed timestamp meaning leaks an `AttributeError`",
      "description": "`Timestamp` does not validate that `meaning` is a `TimeMeaning`. If a caller constructs `Timestamp(100, \"bad\")` and passes it to `SignalEvent`, this check correctly detects that the meaning is not `AVAILABLE_AT`, but formatting the error accesses `self.time.meaning.value` and raises `AttributeError` instead of `InvalidSignalError`. Validate the meaning\u2019s type before formatting it, and cover this case with a test.",
